From 14314261453daef76b4a4b72884f51c9c62c66ae Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 23:57:03 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 2/5] fix(post): restate A after every G30 on the microARC 4
 (review of PR #798)

The bare G30 before every T.. M6 moves every axis to the stored G30
position under LinuxCNC (params 5181-5189), A included, but the post kept
the A word it last wrote and skipped the index when the next section sat
on the same face. Two operations on one face (a rough and a finish at
A90, or T3 then T4) posted the second with no G0 A.., cutting wherever
G30 left the table.

The post now forgets the held A when it writes G30, and at every section
end, so every section opens with G53 G0 Z / G0 A.. - a same-tool
continuation too (a section boundary is where an operator may stop and
jog). The 4-face golden and the kit program are unchanged: every op
there indexed already.

Pinned by a_tool_change_on_the_same_face_restates_a_after_the_g30 and
a_same_tool_continuation_on_the_same_face_restates_a (both fail before).

Also: the kit README warns that the safe Z is the top of travel (confirm
the part/chuck/jaw swept radius clears the tool there) and that each G30
can move A; checklist item 7 no longer claims A ends at 0. The parser's
head search gets a direct test (mch_head_search.rs), and find_type's doc
comment is back on find_type.

Refs #785

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX
