From 31acc320b02887747292551afe2e406ef7502152 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 00:57:36 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 4/5] feat(app): refuse an A index whose retracted tool can't
 clear the swept work

Before a 4th axis that turns the work indexes, the post lifts Z to the
safe retract and turns A under the tool. The program gate now checks
that the tool tip there clears the radius the stock, the parts and the
turning fixtures sweep about the A centerline, with a 5 mm margin, and
refuses the post by name otherwise (op, A, tip height, swept radius,
clearance).

- .mch: a work-turning rotary (no head below it) may state nose_to_axis,
  the spindle nose's height above its centerline at safe_retract. The
  microARC 4 file states 10.6 in (770MX 13.75 in nose to table less the
  microARC's 3.15 in centre height). Unstated on a work-turning A about
  X refuses by name.
- posting::index_swing: the gate clause; machines with no work-turning A
  (and head tilts) are untouched.
- The tester-kit .camproj is re-saved with the new machine facts; the kit
  .nc is byte-identical.

Fixes #804

