From 7a803d0f1901dbb2fc5f1f5965e6bb04b1c826c0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 01:35:39 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] fix(app): judge a table A with no axis vector; name
 pre-#804 machines on load

Follow-ups to the #804 index-swing check (PR #810 review):

- A work-turning rotary with no axis vector was not judged, a silent
  pass. It now takes its RS-274 letter's line: an A is about X and is
  judged like the microARC's. One with no vector and no RS-274 rotary
  letter refuses every op by name, asking for its axis.
- AxisLimits::turns_part is Option<bool>: a parsed rotary always states
  it, so a rotary read back without the key was saved before #804.
  Opening such a project adds a load note naming the machine and the
  rotary and asking for the machine to be reloaded.
- The microARC tester kit README says to keep the stored G30 Z at the
  top of travel; assets/machines/AGENTS.md documents the axis rule.
- Decision record: docs/decisions/813-swing-gaps.md.

Fixes #813

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX
